# TPM2 support in systemd itself, for the hardened images.
#
# NOT the same thing as app-crypt/tpm2-tools, which these profiles have
# shipped all along (amdkdehard.conf PROF_LIVE_PKGS). tpm2-tools is the CLI;
# USE=tpm is what puts TPM2 into systemd's own paths — systemd-cryptenroll
# --tpm2-device, systemd-pcrlock, the measured-boot units, and the
# /usr/lib/udev/tpm2_id callout.
#
# That callout is why this file exists. systemd installs
# /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60-tpm2-id.rules UNCONDITIONALLY, but the tpm2_id
# binary it calls only gets built with USE=tpm. On a machine with a TPM the
# result is an error at every boot and no TPM2 device properties in udev:
#
#   (udev-worker): tpmrm0: Failed to find and pin callout binary
#   "/usr/lib/udev/tpm2_id": No such file or directory
#
# Observed on the installed nvidiahard system 2026-08-13 (bootctl reports
# "TPM2 Support: yes"), which is a stock build of this profile — so it is a
# profile-level gap, not host drift.
#
# Cost: one dependency, app-crypt/tpm2-tss (systemd-261.1.ebuild:102).
# Placed in the 'hardened' layer rather than 'common' because it is these
# profiles that carry the TPM2/PCR material from intro-hardening.md.
sys-apps/systemd tpm
